<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a null pointer dereference in the `lwan_shutdown` function in the `lwan` project. Specifically, the `l->config.ssl.cert` pointer is NULL, but it is passed to `strlen` without a prior null check. This happens because the `lwan_init` function does not initialize this pointer when a configuration file is not found, and the fuzzer does not provide one.

A potential fix would be to add a null check before calling `strlen` on `l->config.ssl.cert` in `lwan.c`:

```c
if (l->config.ssl.cert) {
lwan_always_bzero(l->config.ssl.cert, strlen(l->config.ssl.cert));
}
```

This would prevent the crash when the SSL certificate path is not configured.
</crash-analysis>

